// RtOp, text: Text, numbers, regular expressions, panics and `std.base64`. Read by `compiler/kir/build.rs`.
StrLen,
StrIsEmpty,
StrUpper,
StrLower,
StrTrim,
StrContains,
StrStartsWith,
StrEndsWith,
StrRepeat,
WrappingAdd,
WrappingSub,
WrappingMul,
CheckedAdd,
CheckedSub,
CheckedMul,
CheckedDiv,
/// More methods of text and lists (spec 14.2).
StrReplace,
StrLines,
StrChars,
StrIndexOf,
StrSlice,
MathSqrt,
MathPow,
MathFloor,
MathCeil,
MathRound,
/// `std.regex` (spec 14.8). Compiling can fail.
RegexNew,
RegexAdvanced,
RegexIsMatch,
RegexFind,
RegexFindAll,
RegexCaptures,
RegexNamedCaptures,
RegexReplace,
RegexReplaceAll,
RegexSplit,
StrSplit,
StrBytes,
/// A `Float`'s IEEE 754 bits and back (spec 14.2): the slot already
/// holds them, so the runtime gives its operand back.
FloatBits,
FloatFromBits,
/// `panic(message)` with a message computed while the program runs
/// (spec 5.6); a written-out message is `ExprKind::Panic`.
PanicText,
/// `a ** b` for whole numbers of the result's type (spec 1.8): panics
/// when `b` is negative or the result doesn't fit.
IntPow,
/// `a.near(b)` on floats (spec 14.2).
FloatNear,
/// `d.round(places)` (`c` is 0) and `d.round_even(places)` (`c` is 1)
/// on a `Decimal` (spec 14.2).
DecRound,
/// `match` on an `Error` (spec 5.5): the error it holds, past any
/// `context`, as the optional of the result's type: `none` when it is
/// of another type.
ErrorAs,
/// `std.base64` (spec 14.20): `encode` (data, URL-safe, padded) and
/// `decode` (text, URL-safe), which can fail.
Base64Encode,
Base64Decode,
